    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0055" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/8–1546: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Durbrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-08-15T12:00:00+03:00">August 15,
                            1946—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 15—7:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3202. Printed document has been received by British Embassy here from London
                    containing report of British Ambassador at Nanking regarding conversation with
                    Chou En-lai, Communist representative <pb facs="0056" n="46" xml:id="pg46"/> at
                    Nanking. Chou reportedly complained to Ambassador of American interference in
                    China and support of KMT.</p>
                <p>He was said to have suggested that Ambassador recommend to Bevin<anchor n="48"
                        xml:id="d17-f1"/> that Bevin and Molotov<anchor n="49" xml:id="d17-f2"/>
                    call Byrnes to account for violation of Moscow Foreign Ministers Agreement on
                        China.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d17-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated to London 344; Paris, 303.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d17-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Durbrow</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d17-f1" n="48" xml:id="d17-f1-content">
                <p>Ernest Bevin, British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f2" n="49" xml:id="d17-f2-content">
                <p>V. M. Molotov, Soviet Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f3" n="50" xml:id="d17-f3-content">
                <p>Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, December 30, 1945, p.
                    1030.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f4" n="51" xml:id="d17-f4-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Embassy in China in Department’s telegram No. 611, August 15, 4
                    p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
